WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.033
-You look gorgeous.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.267
Thank you so much
for coming to the show.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.000
-My pleasure.
-It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.767
I was doing a little reading up
about you, and I --

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.200
-What were you reading?
-I was reading the --

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.234
[ Laughter ]
No, great stuff, great stuff.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:13.434
I read that your mom knew
you were gonna be a star.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.601
-Yeah, yeah.
-At a young age.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:16.968
You were in front of the TV --

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:18.133
-You about to get me
in trouble, Jimmy.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.501
-No, no, no.
-No, you are,

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:22.033
because it's been a thing.
She saw me watching TV,

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:24.267
watching "Soul Train,"
and she said I was dancing.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:27.634
The contention is whether
I was 2 or 4.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:30.167
I've been saying 4,
and I get home, and she's like,

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.434
"Danielle, you're on the TV,
and you're telling the people

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.300
the wrong thing. It's 2."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.501
And I'm like, "My bad."
Sorry, Mom.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:37.868
[ Both laugh ]
-So you were 2?

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:40.000
-So somewhere between 2 and 4.
-So you're 2 years old,

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.000
watching Don Cornelius
on "Soul Train"...

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.033
-And I was grooving
and grooving, and she said,

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.033
"That baby needs to be
in performing arts."

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.734
So she put me in dance,
and it was my first medium.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.200
And I started doing theater

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.567
and just moving into
all the other things.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.200
Experimental stuff,
performing arts,

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:55.634
you know, just everything.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.534
And so it's just been a part
of my life since I was a kid.

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.767
-Yeah, and so I go,
that's amazing, I love that.

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.434
You watch "Soul Train,"
it gets you, and you go,

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.834
"That's my acting bug."
But then I heard that you

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.767
watched a film like a hundred
times in a row, 'cause it was --

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.701
-It's not a hundred!
That's an exaggeration.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.467
-Mom?
Mom, are you watching, Mom?

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.367
-No! Don't you --
She don't know!

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.901
I was by myself!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.367
-How many times
did you watch this film?

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:21.167
-It was at least like 20 to 30
times the summer it came out.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.434
It was "Lord of the Rings" one.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:24.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.734
Right? Right?
-Now, that's the one.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.934
-When the DVD came out.
-And that was the one.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.467
And that -- you said,
"That's it right there.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:32.367
This is a film.
This is a masterpiece.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.400
This is what I gotta do."

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.300
-Specifically, Gollum.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:40.834
Andy Serkis as Gollum,
as Smeagol, is just --

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:44.300
you know, it's divine.
It's vocality, it's physicality,

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.701
it's all of the things,
and so --

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.868
-That performance changed
the game in your head.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.601
-Yeah, yeah.
-And you memorized

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.334
Gollum's moves and how Gollum --

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.868
Can you talk like Gollum?
-Yes.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.300
Yes, I can.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.868
-What would you say as Gollum?
-Well, as Gollum,

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:03.067
